## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to enable rapid domain adaptation with privacy guarantees in a real-time environment, emphasizing latency constraints, privacy preservation, and robust rollback mechanisms.

## Key Concepts

- Parameter-efficient adapters (LoRA/Adapters) for domain adaptation
- On-device fine-tuning with privacy guarantees (DP or federated learning)
- Streaming drift detection and safe rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: load base model, attach adapter for domain, fine-tune on small labeled set
function adaptDomain(model, domain, labeledData) {
  const adapter = new LoRAAdapter(model, { rank: 4, alpha: 8 });
  adapter.fineTune(labeledData, { privacy: 'DP-SGD', epochs: 3 });
  return adapter;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a multilingual, latency-constrained moderation system with privacy, drift detection, and staged rollout.

## Key Concepts
- On-deviceQuantized models and fast feature extraction
- Cross-language evaluation and fairness
- Drift detection, versioning, rollback, and explainability

## Code Example
```javascript
// On-device feature extraction (3-grams) - illustrative
function extractFeatures(text) {
  const t = text.toLowerCase();
  const grams = {}; 
  for (let i = 0; i < t.length - 2; i++) {
    const g = t.slice(i, i + 3);
    grams[g] = (grams[g] || 0) + 1;
  }
  return grams;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify and respond to drift in multilingual data?
- What would you log for compliance while preserving user privacy?

## Why This Is Asked
